X:1
T:The Wild Rover
C:Traditional (Roud 1173)
S:Melody after a transcription in C by Alf Warnock (folktunefinder.com, tune 105100); no printed source cited
N:Transposed from C to G for baritones. Written in treble clef; men sing an octave below written pitch (D3 to D4).
N:The source is an instrumental waltz setting with no words; the fit of the words is my own.
N:Bars 5 and 15: one quarter split into two eighths of the same pitch for "And I". Bar 17: "wild" held over two notes.
N:Bars 23-24: the source's run (D E F# G) falls where the four claps go; instruments play it, singers clap.
N:Bar 19 chord added (the source marks none there). Sing the chorus after each verse; verses 2-4 are printed below.
M:3/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=180
K:G
